From 1ed55f10b27a1cf36eae742e91df029a5a47319b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:54:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 186/194] glm_moe_dsa: int8 KV snapshots keep both scale planes
 of every row

With TF_GLM_KV8_INT8=1 the dsa's 576-wide rows carry two FP32 scales a row
(tf_glm_lat_write_i8_w576 writes scales[2*at] and scales[2*at+1]), but the
snapshot plan (cuda_snapshot_layout.zig Plan.rows) kept at * 4 bytes of the
scale plane with a page_rows * 4 span, and the disk image (cuda_disk_image.zig
Shape) counted 4 bytes a row: a kept or saved prefix lost the scales of every
row from at/2 on, so a restored prompt-cache state read wrong scales there.

latent.scaleBytes(lw) is now the one rule (8 on the dsa's int8 rows, 4 on
E4M3) for cacheBytes, the snapshot plan's scale part and span, and the disk
image's scale bytes and row. Paged and KV-shard layouts are E4M3 only (int8 is
the dsa's, whose 8-bit rows are never on pages) and keep 4.

Test: cuda_kv8_snapshot_test.zig fills distinct codes and scales (both int8
planes), keeps a 1536-row prefix through the real Plan and Pool (device and
host tiers), overwrites the live rows, restores, and compares every code and
scale byte below and above at/2, for dsa int8 and E4M3 in the arena, Flash
E4M3 in the arena and on pages; plus the disk image's int8 byte count. Before
this change the int8 case loses 3072 rows' scales (4 caches x 768) and the
image counts no second plane; after it every byte matches.

Found in Codex's analysis report (docs/gpt-sol-new.md, section 6.3).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
